{
 "translation": "When I was returning to the veranda with faltering steps, head bowed, I saw Zameer with a long parcel. He was taking out a new racket for himself from it. She herself was engrossed in looking at the sparkle of the ring on her finger. She laughed, but my ears, far from my body, were hearing a song of death somewhere, and my eyes were seeing thousands of funeral processions passing in the air.",
